.TH UNLOADMOD 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
unloadmod \- Unload a module from a region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unloadmod
.I name
.RI [ region ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Unload the game module
.I name
from a region, where its commands and event handlers stop running. Modules
are named by stem only: a name containing a slash is refused.
.PP
The region is a bare world number (0\-65535) or the keyword \fBcosmos\fP,
under exactly the same rules as every other region selector. Without one the
command acts on your \fBdefault target region\fP (see \fBtarget\fP(10)), or
on the region you are standing in if you have set none. Regions at other
widths (districts, super\-planet regions \-\- see \fBgrant\fP(10)) are
reached through your default; see \fBtarget\fP(10) for the width\-and\-point
form.
.PP
As with \fBloadmod\fP, this needs exact ownership of the named region, and
the module must be loaded there: unloading what was never loaded says so.
The removal persists in the region's row and survives the next boot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loadmod,modlist,release,target,planet (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
